## CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS

### Structure
1. **Layout Shell** - The system already provides the `<body>` wrapper plus the interface/navigation containers. Your response MUST begin with the page wrapper `<div class="flex justify-center items-start min-h-[calc(100dvh-100px)]">` and include the nested content container `<div id="content" ...>`. Do **NOT** output `<body>`, `<div id="interface-container">`, or `<div id="nav-container">`.

2. **Single Section** - There MUST be exactly ONE `<section>` tag in the HTML.

3. **Section Attributes**:
   - `role="article"` for narrative/informational content
   - `role="activity"` for interactive/exercise content
   - `data-section-type` attribute with the provided section type (e.g., `data-section-type="text-and-images"`)

### Text & Data IDs
4. **All text elements** MUST have a `data-id` attribute matching the provided text ID.

5. **Text must be direct children** - Elements with `data-id` MUST contain plain text as immediate children:
   - ✅ CORRECT: `<p data-id="text-1-0">This is text</p>`
   - ✅ CORRECT: `<strong><p data-id="text-1-0">This is text</p></strong>`
   - ❌ WRONG: `<p data-id="text-1-0"><strong>This is text</strong></p>`

6. **Use provided IDs only** - DO NOT create additional data-ids beyond those provided.

### Images
7. **Only provided images** - DO NOT add placeholder images or any `<img>` tags without a corresponding image ID.

8. **All images need data-id** - Every `<img>` MUST have `data-id` matching the provided image ID:
   ```html
   <img src="./images/filename.svg" data-id="img-26-2" alt="Description" class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-lg" />
   ```

9. **Appropriate sizing** - Use style guide classes (`max-w-sm`, responsive layouts) to prevent images from dominating the page.

### Activity-Specific Requirements
10. **Sorting Activities (activity_sorting)** - When section type is `activity_sorting`, you MUST:
    - Use `word-card` class (NOT `activity-item`) for draggable items
    - Add BOTH `data-activity-item` AND `data-id` to each word card
    - Use `category` class for drop zones
    - Add `data-activity-category` attribute to each category
    - Include `<ul class="word-list"></ul>` inside each category
    - See "Sorting Activity Structure" in style guide for complete example

11. **Multiple Matching Activities (activity_multiple_matching)** - When section type is `activity_multiple_matching`, you MUST:
    - Group items in columns using `data-column-index` attributes
    - Use `activity-item` class for draggable items with color-coded backgrounds per column
    - Add `data-activity-item`, `data-column-index`, and `data-id` to each draggable item
    - Use `dropzone` class for drop zones
    - Include `<div role="region" class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2"></div>` inside each drop zone
    - Add numbered labels using `<p class="text-lg font-bold">1.</p>` inside each drop zone
    - See "Multiple Matching Activity Structure" in style guide for complete example

### Styling & Components
12. **Follow the style guide** - Reference the included style guide above for all styling patterns, components, and color choices.

### Content Rules
13. **Text modification** - You MAY slightly truncate or exclude text for pedagogical reasons, but you MUST:
    - Remove the entire element AND its data-id if excluding text
    - Never split a data-id across multiple elements
    - Preserve the meaning and flow

14. **Language** - For `textarea` and `input` placeholder text, use this language: {{ language }}

15. **Accessibility** - Include proper `aria-label`, `role`, and semantic HTML. Ensure readable contrast as specified in the style guide.

